/-- **Lemma 3.1 (Nishimori identity).**
Z. Li, *Efficient Posterior Sampling for ℤ₂ Synchronization*, arXiv:2610.08199 (held version,
sha256 536ad4d8…), Lemma 3.1, p.14: "Let `ℱ` be the sigma-field generated by the observations being retained.
Conditional on `ℱ`, let `σ¹, …, σ^{a+1}` be independent samples from `ℒ(θ | ℱ)`, independent also of
`θ` conditionally on `ℱ`. For every bounded function `f` of `a + 1` configurations, which may also
depend measurably on `ℱ`, `E[⟨f(θ, σ¹, …, σ^a)⟩ | ℱ] = ⟨f(σ^{a+1}, σ¹, …, σ^a)⟩`. In particular,
`R_{1θ}` and `R_{12}` have the same distribution after averaging over the observations. The identity
remains valid when the retained observations include revealed coordinates of `θ`."

**Formalization Note.** First conjunct: a finite signal `θ ∈ Θ` with prior `π`, observed through a
Markov kernel `κ` into a measurable space `O` (the retained observations, which may include revealed
coordinates of `θ`, so the last sentence is covered); `⟨·⟩` is the posterior average of independent
replicas (Bayes weights `postWeight`). The conditional-expectation identity given `ℱ = σ(o)` is
stated in its integrated form: equality of the integrals over `{o ∈ B}` for every measurable `B`
(the right side is `ℱ`-measurable, so this is equivalent). `f` is bounded and measurable in `o`.
Second conjunct: in the Gaussian model of §3.1, for every `N`, `r, t ≥ 0` and Borel set `U`, the
planted-averaged posterior probabilities of `R_{1θ} ∈ U` and `R_{12} ∈ U` agree. -/
theorem lemma_3_1 :
    (∀ (Θ O : Type) [Fintype Θ] [DecidableEq Θ] [MeasurableSpace Θ] [DiscreteMeasurableSpace Θ]
      [MeasurableSpace O] (π : Measure Θ) [IsProbabilityMeasure π] (κ : Kernel Θ O)
      [IsMarkovKernel κ] (a : ℕ) (f : Θ → (Fin a → Θ) → O → ℝ),
      (∀ θ σ, Measurable (f θ σ)) → (∃ Cf : ℝ, ∀ θ σ o, |f θ σ o| ≤ Cf) →
      ∀ B : Set O, MeasurableSet B →
        ∫ p in {p : Θ × O | p.2 ∈ B}, postAvg π κ a p.2 (fun σ => f p.1 σ p.2) ∂(π ⊗ₘ κ) =
          ∫ p in {p : Θ × O | p.2 ∈ B}, postAvg π κ (a + 1) p.2
            (fun σ => f (σ (Fin.last a)) (fun j => σ j.castSucc) p.2) ∂(π ⊗ₘ κ)) ∧
    (∀ (N : ℕ) (r t : ℝ), 0 ≤ r → 0 ≤ t → ∀ U : Set ℝ, MeasurableSet U →
      ∫⁻ ω, ENNReal.ofReal (lawMean (gpost r t ω) fun σ => U.indicator 1 (overlap σ ω.1))
          ∂(gaussLaw N) =
        ∫⁻ ω, ENNReal.ofReal (avg2 (gpost r t ω) fun σ τ => U.indicator 1 (overlap σ τ))
          ∂(gaussLaw N)) := by sorry

end Z2PostSamp
